  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Introduction</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Tank Top Manufacturer for Casual and Activewear Brands</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>As a specialized tank top manufacturer based in Bangladesh, SDF Clothing understands that versatility, comfort, and style are essential requirements for casual and activewear brands. The tank top market spans multiple segments from basic layering pieces to fashion-forward statement items. Our facility delivers on these requirements with minimum orders of 300 pieces, making professional manufacturing accessible to emerging lifestyle brands and established labels expanding their warm-weather collections.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh has developed significant expertise in knit garment manufacturing, with specialized factories focused on jersey knit production for t-shirts and tank tops. Our tank top production leverages this expertise, offering international brands access to skilled labor, competitive pricing, and established supply chains for cotton jersey, bamboo, and modal fabrics. The 300-piece minimum enables brands to test different styles and fabric weights without committing to large inventory positions, reducing risk while accessing factory-direct pricing.</p>
        
        <p>Our tank tops manufacturing addresses the technical requirements that distinguish quality tank tops from basic sleeveless shirts: appropriate fabric weight for drape and opacity, pre-shrunk materials to maintain fit after washing, durable construction that withstands repeated wear, and neckline and armhole finishing that prevents stretching. We work with cotton jersey, bamboo, modal, polyester, and rayon blends to achieve these characteristics while offering options for sustainable materials and various price points.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Product Range</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">What We Manufacture</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our tank tops production encompasses multiple styles and fabric weights designed for different markets, climates, and fashion preferences. Each style maintains our commitment to quality fabrics and durable construction while offering distinct aesthetic and functional characteristics. We manufacture all styles from 300 pieces minimum, with the ability to mix styles within larger orders for comprehensive collections.</p>
        
        <p>Basic tank tops feature standard armholes and a simple neckline, typically crew or scoop neck, for versatile casual wear. These styles use mid-weight fabrics in the 160-180 GSM range, providing structure without excessive weight. The basic tank is a wardrobe staple that works as a layering piece or standalone item in warm weather. Armhole depth is carefully calibrated to provide coverage while maintaining a sleeveless silhouette. Basic tank tops are popular in essentials collections and for customers seeking simple, versatile pieces.</p>
        
        <p>Racerback tank tops feature straps that converge toward the center back, creating an athletic silhouette that provides enhanced shoulder mobility. This style is popular in activewear markets and for customers who engage in fitness activities. Racerback construction requires precise strap alignment to ensure the back design is centered and symmetrical. The racerback configuration also offers visual interest on the back, making these tanks suitable for both athletic and casual wear. Racerback tank tops typically use performance fabrics in the 150-180 GSM range for moisture management during activity.</p>
        
        <p>Muscle tank tops feature wider armholes that extend further down the torso, creating a relaxed, casual silhouette that highlights the shoulders. This style is popular in streetwear and casual markets, particularly among male customers. The wider armholes require careful armhole binding to prevent gaping while maintaining the relaxed aesthetic. Muscle tanks typically use heavier fabrics in the 180-220 GSM range to provide structure and prevent transparency. The muscle tank silhouette has experienced renewed popularity in recent years as part of the oversized casual wear trend.</p>
        
        <p>Flowy tank tops incorporate a relaxed, A-line silhouette that drapes away from the body, providing a feminine and comfortable fit. These styles often use lighter-weight fabrics in the 140-160 GSM range to enhance drape and movement. The flowy silhouette requires pattern adjustments to ensure the garment maintains its shape while providing the intended relaxed fit. Flowy tanks are popular in women's casual wear and resort collections, appealing to customers who prioritize comfort and ease of wear. The relaxed fit also accommodates a range of body types comfortably.</p>
        
        <p>Cropped tank tops feature a shortened length that typically ends above the natural waistline, creating a contemporary silhouette popular in fashion-forward markets. Cropped lengths can vary from just above the waist to significantly cropped styles that end at the ribcage. These styles require careful proportioning to ensure the cropped length is flattering across different torso lengths. Cropped tank tops are popular in streetwear, festival fashion, and for customers who follow current fashion trends. The cropped silhouette pairs well with high-waisted bottoms for balanced styling.</p>
        
        <p>Yoga tank tops combine the sleeveless silhouette of tank tops with performance features suitable for yoga and fitness activities. These styles often include built-in shelf bras, racerback configurations for shoulder mobility, and moisture-wicking fabrics. Yoga tanks typically use performance blends in the 150-180 GSM range with stretch for unrestricted movement. The construction focuses on flat seams to prevent chafing during activity and secure strap construction to prevent slipping. Yoga tank tops bridge the gap between activewear and casual wear, suitable for both practice and everyday use.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Style</th>
              <th>Fabric GSM</th>
              <th>Key Features</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Price Tier</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Basic Tank Top</td>
