  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Production Process</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Our Manufacturing Process</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Our tank tops manufacturing follows a structured process designed to ensure consistent fit, fabric quality, and construction durability. The process typically spans 60-75 days for first-time orders including sampling and production, with 45-60 days for repeat orders using approved fabrics and patterns. Tank tops require particular attention to neckline and armhole finishing to prevent stretching and maintain shape through wear.</p>
        
        <p>The process begins with specification review, where we analyze your requirements including fabric preferences (cotton jersey, bamboo, modal, or polyester), style type (basic, racerback, muscle, or flowy), size chart, neckline preference, and hem finish. Our team provides feedback on technical feasibility and may suggest modifications to optimize manufacturability while maintaining design intent. This stage takes 2-3 days and ensures technical alignment before sampling begins. For tank tops, we pay particular attention to armhole depth and neckline drop specifications.</p>
        
        <p>Fabric sourcing and pre-shrinking follows specification review, taking 10-15 days for standard fabrics and 15-20 days for custom fabric development. Tank top fabrics undergo pre-shrinking treatment before cutting to minimize dimensional changes after washing. We test fabrics for shrinkage in both warp and weft directions, ensuring that finished garments maintain their measurements after laundering. If you require custom fabric development for specific colors or weights, we coordinate with mills to produce sample yardage for testing and approval.</p>
        
        <p>Sample development for tank tops takes 15-20 days. Initial samples focus on construction and basic fit, with subsequent samples refining neckline shape, armhole depth, and overall length. We provide detailed measurement reports comparing samples to your specifications and conduct wash testing to verify dimensional stability. Tank top samples require particular attention to neckline binding and armhole finishing to ensure they maintain their shape through wear and washing. You may request multiple sample rounds to perfect the design.</p>
        
        <p>Neckline and armhole testing is a critical step in tank top sampling that we conduct on all samples. We test neckline elasticity to ensure it stretches for easy on/off without becoming permanently stretched out. Armhole openings are evaluated for appropriate coverage and shape retention. For racerback styles, we verify strap alignment and back design symmetry. This testing ensures that the fit customers experience initially is maintained through wear and washing, reducing returns due to stretched necklines or distorted armholes.</p>
        
        <p>Pattern grading for tank tops requires careful attention to proportional scaling, particularly for armhole and neckline dimensions. The relationship between neckline width, armhole depth, and body measurements must be maintained through grading to ensure consistent fit across sizes. Our pattern makers use graded measurement systems that account for this relationship, producing size sets from XS to 4XL that maintain proportional fit. Grading takes 3-5 days and includes verification of armhole scaling, neckline proportionality, and length consistency across sizes.</p>
        
        <p>Bulk production for tank tops spans 30-40 days from fabric receipt, with complex styles such as racerback or flowy designs requiring 35-45 days. Cutting is performed with attention to grain direction to ensure consistent drape and minimize torque. Sewing lines are staffed by operators trained in jersey garment construction, with particular expertise in neckline binding, armhole finishing, and hem construction. Quality checkpoints at each sewing operation verify seam integrity, stitch consistency, and finish quality. Throughout production, we conduct in-line testing of neckline elasticity and armhole shape.</p>
        
        <p>Final quality inspection uses AQL 2.5 standards for major defects and AQL 4.0 for minor defects, with additional testing for tank top-specific criteria. Inspection includes measurement verification against graded size charts, wash testing on random samples to verify dimensional stability, and neckline elasticity testing. We also conduct visual inspection of neckline and armhole finishing to ensure clean, consistent construction. Detailed inspection reports with photos are provided before shipment, and any defects found are rectified before goods leave our facility.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Materials</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Fabric & Material Options</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Fabric selection is critical to tank top performance, affecting comfort, drape, durability, and care requirements. We offer multiple fabric options optimized for different climates, seasons, and performance requirements. All fabrics are pre-shrunk and tested for dimensional stability to ensure consistent fit after laundering.</p>
        
        <p>Cotton jersey is the traditional choice for tank tops, providing natural comfort, breathability, and softness against the skin. Cotton jersey typically ranges from 140-180 GSM, with lighter weights for summer and heavier weights for year-round wear. The fabric has natural stretch and recovery, though less than synthetic blends, providing a comfortable fit without excessive cling. Cotton jersey is breathable and absorbs moisture, making it comfortable in warm weather. We offer combed cotton jersey for enhanced softness and reduced pilling. Cotton jersey is our recommendation for classic tank top styling and customers prioritizing natural fibers.</p>
        
        <p>Bamboo fabric offers sustainable softness with natural performance characteristics. Bamboo viscose is produced from bamboo grass, a rapidly renewable resource, and features a luxurious hand feel similar to silk. Bamboo fabrics typically range from 140-160 GSM and are naturally moisture-wicking and antimicrobial, reducing odor buildup during wear. The fabric has excellent drape, creating flowing silhouettes ideal for women's tank tops. Bamboo is more sustainable than conventional cotton, requiring less water and no pesticides. Bamboo fabrics cost approximately 10-15% more than cotton jersey but appeal to eco-conscious customers.</p>
        
        <p>Modal is a semi-synthetic fiber produced from beech wood pulp, offering luxurious softness with excellent drape and color retention. Modal typically ranges from 150-180 GSM and resists pilling and fading better than cotton. The fabric has a smooth, silky hand feel and maintains its shape through repeated washing. Modal is breathable and moisture-wicking, making it comfortable for warm weather wear. The beech wood used for modal is harvested from sustainably managed forests, making modal an eco-friendly option. Modal is ideal for premium positioning and customers seeking luxurious feel with practical performance.</p>
        
        <p>Polyester jersey offers durability, color retention, and cost efficiency at competitive prices. Polyester typically ranges from 140-180 GSM and maintains its appearance through repeated washing without significant fading or pilling. The synthetic fiber resists shrinkage, reducing dimensional stability concerns. Polyester jersey is lighter weight than cotton for equivalent coverage, making it suitable for warm weather. However, polyester does not provide the natural hand feel of cotton and may retain odors more than natural fibers. Polyester jersey is ideal for value positioning and performance-focused tank tops.</p>
        
        <p>Rayon blends combine rayon with cotton or polyester for enhanced drape and fluid movement. Rayon is a semi-synthetic fiber produced from wood pulp, offering excellent drape and a soft hand feel. Blends typically range from 150-190 GSM and balance the natural comfort of cotton with the enhanced drape of rayon. Rayon blends are particularly suitable for flowy tank top styles where drape is a priority. The fabric requires careful care to maintain appearance, which should be communicated to end consumers. Rayon blends are ideal for fashion-forward tank tops with feminine silhouettes.</p>
        
        <p>Organic cotton jersey, certified by GOTS (Global Organic Textile Standard), provides sustainable options for customers prioritizing organic materials. Organic cotton is grown without synthetic pesticides or fertilizers and processed without harmful chemicals. The fabric maintains the same comfort and performance as conventional cotton jersey with the added benefit of environmental certification. Organic cotton typically costs 15-20% more than conventional cotton but enables sustainability claims that appeal to eco-conscious consumers. GOTS certification requires traceability throughout the supply chain.</p>
        
        <p>Performance blends incorporating spandex (typically 5-10%) provide enhanced stretch and recovery for activewear tank tops. These blends maintain the comfort of cotton or polyester with added stretch for unrestricted movement during fitness activities. Performance blends typically range from 150-180 GSM and are ideal for yoga tanks, running tanks, and other activewear applications. The spandex component requires special care in construction to ensure even distribution and prevent seam popping. Performance blends are ideal for athletic markets and customers seeking enhanced mobility.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-wrapper">
        <table class="comparison">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Fabric</th>
              <th>GSM Range</th>
              <th>Key Properties</th>
              <th>Best For</th>
              <th>Price Tier</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Cotton Jersey</td>
              <td>140-180</td>
              <td>Natural, breathable, soft, classic</td>
              <td>Basic tanks, essentials, casual</td>
              <td>$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Bamboo</td>
              <td>140-160</td>
              <td>Sustainable, antimicrobial, luxurious</td>
              <td>Eco-conscious, premium women's</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Modal</td>
              <td>150-180</td>
              <td>Luxurious, drape, color-fast, pill-resistant</td>
              <td>Premium, fashion, flowy styles</td>
              <td>$$$</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="comparison__row--highlight">
              <td>Polyester Jersey</td>
              <td>140-180</td>
              <td>Durable, color-fast, cost-efficient</td>
