        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Bangladesh Advantage</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Why Source Tank Tops from Bangladesh</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Bangladesh has established itself as a competitive sourcing destination for tank tops and knit garments, combining cost advantages with specialized expertise in jersey knit production. The country's garment industry includes numerous factories focused on t-shirt and tank top manufacturing, with developed supply chains for cotton jersey and other knit fabrics. This specialization, combined with competitive labor costs, makes Bangladesh an attractive option for tank top manufacturing.</p>
        
        <p>Labor costs in Bangladesh are significantly lower than in China, Vietnam, or Turkey, translating to 15-25% cost savings on finished tank tops. However, the cost advantage does not come at the expense of quality. The Bangladeshi garment industry has developed particular expertise in jersey garment production, with operators skilled in handling stretch fabrics, binding necklines and armholes, and maintaining consistent stitching on lightweight materials. Our facility conducts regular training programs to ensure operators are proficient in the latest tank top construction techniques.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh's domestic fabric supply includes numerous knitting mills capable of producing cotton jersey, bamboo, modal, and polyester blends suitable for tank top construction. The country has invested heavily in circular knitting capacity, reducing reliance on imported fabrics for basic tank top styles. This local sourcing reduces lead times and logistics costs compared to countries that rely entirely on imported fabrics. Our relationships with local knitting mills ensure priority allocation and consistent quality for tank top fabrics. For specialized fabrics or custom weights, we maintain relationships with international fabric suppliers.</p>
        
        <p>The country's export infrastructure includes experienced freight forwarders, customs brokers, and documentation specialists familiar with garment export requirements. Shipments from Bangladesh to major markets are routine, with multiple weekly sailings to Europe and North America. Ocean freight is particularly cost-effective for tank tops given the lightweight nature of the garments, allowing efficient container utilization. The established export infrastructure reduces the risk of delays and documentation errors that can occur with less experienced sourcing locations.</p>
        
        <p>Bangladesh's garment industry looks very different on workplace safety and social compliance today than it did before the reforms that followed 2013. Our facility holds BSCI certification, demonstrating adherence to standards on fair wages, reasonable working hours, and safe working conditions. For tank top and basics brands running high-volume orders, that kind of documented compliance is increasingly what retailers and consumers expect before they'll commit — and it's a big part of why the reputational risk once tied to Bangladesh sourcing has fallen sharply.</p>
        
        <p>Duty-free access to European markets through the Everything But Arms (EBA) arrangement provides Bangladesh garments with preferential tariff treatment, reducing import costs for EU customers. Similar preferential access exists for other markets including Canada, Australia, and Japan. This duty advantage can significantly impact landed costs for tank tops, which are subject to standard garment duty rates in many markets. For brands targeting EU distribution, the duty savings can offset other costs and improve overall margins.</p>
        
        <p>The Bangladesh garment industry has developed specialized expertise in knit garment production, which directly translates to tank top manufacturing. Handling jersey fabrics, binding necklines and armholes, and constructing garments that maintain dimensional stability are well-established skills in the country's workforce. This specialized expertise reduces the learning curve for new tank top styles and ensures consistent quality across production runs. The industry's experience with international casual wear brands also means that quality expectations for fit and finish are well-understood.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">International Shipping</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Shipping to UK, USA, Australia & EU</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>We ship tank tops to major international markets including the United Kingdom, United States, Australia, and European Union countries. Each market has specific requirements for documentation, duties, and shipping timelines that we navigate routinely. Our experience with international tank top shipments ensures your goods arrive on time and with proper documentation for customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>Shipments to the United Kingdom typically take 30-35 days by ocean freight, including transit time and customs clearance. Air freight options reduce this to 7-10 days at significantly higher cost. The UK applies import duties on garments from Bangladesh, though rates vary by fabric composition and declared value. Tank tops typically fall under specific HS codes for cotton or synthetic t-shirts and tank tops. We provide accurate classification and valuation to ensure proper duty calculation. Post-Brexit documentation requirements are handled to ensure smooth customs clearance.</p>
        
        <p>United States shipments take 25-30 days by ocean freight to West Coast ports and 35-40 days to East Coast ports. Air freight takes 5-7 days to major US airports. The US maintains normal trade relations with Bangladesh, with standard MFN duty rates applying to tank tops. The US has specific labeling requirements for garments including fiber content in English and country of origin. We ensure all labels meet US Federal Trade Commission requirements. US customs may also inspect for compliance with textile fiber identification rules, which we address through proper documentation.</p>
        
        <p>Tank top shipments to Australia go by ocean freight in 20-25 days to Sydney, Melbourne, or Brisbane, or by air in 7-10 days when speed matters more than cost. Bangladesh's free trade agreement with Australia eliminates duties on most garment categories provided origin rules are satisfied, and we build that into how we run production. Because Australia enforces strict biosecurity checks, we handle packaging and documentation carefully to keep shipments clear of delays.</p>
        
        <p>Tank top exports to the EU clear duty-free under the Everything But Arms arrangement for least-developed countries. Ocean freight takes 28-32 days to Northern European ports and 32-38 days to Southern European ports, with a 5-8 day air freight alternative. EU-bound documentation includes certificates of origin, detailed commercial invoices, and conformity declarations where required, plus textile labels stating fiber content percentages and care instructions in the destination country's language.</p>
        
        <p>Documentation for all markets includes commercial invoices, packing lists, bills of lading, certificates of origin, and any required certificates for regulated materials. For tank tops, this may include certificates for fiber content if organic or sustainable materials are used. We provide all documentation in English and can arrange for translations if required by specific markets. Our documentation is prepared to meet both customs requirements and your internal accounting needs, with clear descriptions and accurate valuations.</p>
        
        <p>Incoterms can be structured according to your preferences, including FOB (Free On Board) Bangladesh for maximum control, CIF (Cost, Insurance, Freight) to destination port for convenience, or DDP (Delivered Duty Paid) for complete door-to-door service. For tank tops, we typically recommend FOB for experienced importers, as the cost savings on ocean freight for lightweight garments make FOB economically advantageous. CIF and DDP options are available for brands seeking simplified logistics or those new to international sourcing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section__container">
      <div class="section__header">
        <span class="section__label">Certifications</span>
        <div class="accent-line"></div>
        <h2 class="section__title">Quality Standards & Certifications</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="section__text">
        <p>Quality assurance and certification are fundamental to our tank tops manufacturing process. Tank tops require particular attention to dimensional stability and construction durability due to their lightweight nature and frequent wear in warm conditions. We maintain multiple certifications that verify our commitment to quality, social responsibility, and environmental standards.</p>
        
        <p>OEKO-TEX Standard 100 certification applies to our fabrics, ensuring they are free from harmful substances including heavy metals, pesticides, and formaldehyde. This certification is particularly important for tank tops that have prolonged skin contact during warm weather wear. OEKO-TEX testing covers all fabric components including base materials, elastics, trims, and threads. We provide OEKO-TEX certificates for each material lot, enabling you to substantiate claims about chemical safety in your marketing materials.</p>
        
        <p>GOTS (Global Organic Textile Standard) certification applies to our organic cotton fabrics, verifying organic fiber content and ensuring environmentally and socially responsible production. GOTS covers the entire supply chain from harvesting to labeling, ensuring that organic claims are substantiated throughout production. If you choose organic cotton for your tank tops, GOTS certification provides credibility for organic marketing claims and is required by many retailers for organic textile products.</p>
        
        <p>FSC (Forest Stewardship Council) certification applies to our bamboo fabrics, verifying that the bamboo is sourced from responsibly managed forests that provide environmental, social, and economic benefits. FSC certification ensures that bamboo production meets strict standards for sustainable forestry. If you choose bamboo for your tank tops, FSC certification provides credibility for sustainability claims and appeals to environmentally conscious consumers.</p>
        
        <p>Our BSCI (Business Social Compliance Initiative) certification, audited by independent third parties, covers fair wages, reasonable working hours, prohibition of child labor, and safe working conditions across the facility. For tank top and basics programs running large repeat volumes, that's a standing piece of documentation you can share with stakeholders without having to re-verify it on every order — proof of supply chain responsibility that's checked on a recurring cycle rather than a one-off claim.</p>
        
        <p>ISO 9001 certification applies to our quality management system, ensuring consistent processes for production and quality control. ISO 9001 requires documented procedures for all critical processes, regular internal audits, and continuous improvement. This certification provides assurance that our quality systems are systematic and repeatable, reducing variability between production runs. For tank tops, this means consistent fit, fabric quality, and construction across orders.</p>
        
        <p>Internal quality control processes supplement these certifications with day-to-day assurance specific to tank top production. We conduct in-line inspections during production, measuring garments at critical checkpoints to verify dimensional accuracy. Final inspection includes wash testing on random samples to verify dimensional stability, ensuring that garments maintain their fit after home laundering. We maintain records of all testing results, enabling traceability if issues arise after delivery. These internal processes ensure certifications translate to actual quality in finished tank tops.</p>
      </div>
